{
  "resume": "=== Mingyu Huo - Resume.pdf ===\nCarl (Mingyu Huo) \n(929) 319-9980 | Mhuo@schools.nyc.gov  \n\nOBJECTIVE:  To obtain a position as a Secondary Mathematics Teacher \n\nEDUCATION:  Queens College, City University of New York, Flushing, NY \nB. A., Mathematics and Mathematics Education | GPA: 3.755 \n     06/2026  \n\nCERTIFICATION: \n     09/2026  \n\nNew York State Initial Certificate, Mathematics, Grades 7-12 \n\nACADEMIC HONORS: \nFall 2022- \nSpring 2026     Dean’s List \n\nTIME 2000 4-Year Scholarship \n\nRELATED EXPERIENCE: \nSpring 2026  \n                             Bayside High School, Flushing, New York \n\nStudent Teacher \n\n•  Teach Geometry and Foundation of Geometry, and tutor Algebra through Calculus  \n•  Create engaging lesson plans, prepare instructional materials, and grade assessments. \n•  Design and implement differentiated instructions to meet the needs of diverse learners. \n• \n\nParticipated in New York State Science of Reading Micro-credential pilot program and applied research-\nbased literacy practices in mathematics instruction. \n\n    Fall 2025 \nInitial Clinical Experience Student Teacher \n                          East-West School of International Studies, Flushing, New York \n\n•  Team-taught selected mathematics lessons in 7th grade. \n•  Assisted cooperating teacher in differentiating instruction and assessing students. \n\nSpring 2025- \n         Present  \nSubstitute Paraprofessional \n                          Flushing International H.S., Flushing, New York \n\n•  Organize events and manage student data, schedules, and assessments. \n•  Facilitate ESL exams for English language learners. \n\nEXPERIENCE:   \nSpring 2023- \n  Spring 2024   Cashier \n\n99 Cent Store, Flushing, New York \n•  Handled cash transactions and guided customers to locate products. \n•  Verified orders of products and maintained organized well-stocked shelves.  \n\nSKILLS:  \n\nGoogle Classroom, Microsoft Office Suite, Google Workspace, Desmos, Canva, GeoGebra, \nKahoot, Geometry Sketchpad, Smart Notebook; Mandarin & English. \n\nPROFESSIONAL  \nMEMBERSHIP: National Council of Teachers of Mathematics \n\nREFERENCES: Available upon request",
